# F2, 2D asset and SVG creator (12 October 2026)

Status: built and verified both ways on synthetic SVGs. Real reference crop: see the last section.

## What exists

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `ZenRayMotionDesign/zrmd/vector/trace.py` | Deterministic raster to vector, written from the mathematics (no vendored code, no potrace, no vtracer copy). Segmentation into regions joined by small neighbour steps (a gradient stays one region, a hard or blurred edge splits), anti-aliasing slivers absorbed by a two-colour mixing test, colour model per region (flat, linear or radial gradient with stops), stacking by containment, soft coverage target per layer, Gaussian blur estimated from the edge profile, sub-pixel contours, cubic Bezier fitting (Schneider: corners, chord-length parameters, Newton reparameterisation, split at worst point, error bound `fit_error_px` = 0.3 px), then least squares refinement of every control point on the rendered Skia coverage against the target. |
| `zrmd/vector/primitives.py` | Primitive recognition first: circle, ellipse, rect, rounded_rect (fills); line, arc (a full arc is a ring), polyline, stroke_path (strokes, with width, caps). Each candidate is initialised from moments or the skeleton, refined by least squares, accepted only inside the primitive rule (soft IoU >= 0.995, edge mean <= 0.15 px). A wrong primitive fails measurably instead of being forced. |
| `zrmd/vector/asset.py` | `vectorise()` builds params (schema `zrmd/asset2d@1`: palette, layers with kind, geometry, paint, effects blur and opacity, fit measures, shader-bank hints such as `linear_ramp4`, `radial_gradient3`, `glow_gaussian`, `blur_disc_gaussian`). `cook_svg()` bakes params into `asset.svg`, one named `<g id="L02-arc" data-kind="arc">` per layer, gradients in `<defs>`. `evaluate()` gives fidelity (per layer soft IoU and sub-pixel edge distance, composite colour MAE and p99). `write_version()` writes V_NNN, never overwriting. `apply_overrides()` edits by layer id and names an unknown id. Reference crops get `rights: private-1to1`. |
| `Scripts/Vectorise.py` (new this run) | CLI. `trace <image> --id ID [--box x y w h] [--private]` and `rebuild <asset_dir> [--set dotted=value ...] [--overrides FILE] [--source IMAGE]` (HDA loop: edit a value, cook a new version without retracing). |
| `Scripts/VerifySvgTrace.py` | Verifier, 16 workers, `--json`, `--out`, `--write`, `--sabotage`, `--case`. |
| `datasets/vector/synthetic-svg-cases.json` | 16 synthetic SVGs on a 160 x 160 canvas. |
| `settings.json`, section `vector.trace` | Every threshold: tracing, primitives, fidelity (iou_min 0.99, edge_mean_max_px 0.5, colour_mae_max 2.0, colour_p99_max 24), verify (iou_min 0.995, colour_mae_max 1.5, shift_px 1.0, blur_tol 0.15), `raster_ss` 4 (reference rasteriser: Skia at 1x under-covers curved strokes, 1657.2 px against an exact 1664.18). |

Output per asset, under `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/assets2d/<id>/V_NNN/`: `asset.svg`, `params.json`, `render.png`, `fidelity.json`, `version.json`.

