Sabotage run (`--sabotage`: refinement off, forced primitives accepted): exit 1, 17 failed (13 green cases lose fidelity or kinds, 4 wrong-primitive reds are accepted), 5.9 s. Report: `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/docs/build/F2-svg-verify-sabotage.json`.

Editing loop proven: `VerifySvgTrace.py --case logo glow --write` wrote `assets2d/_verify/logo/V_001`, then `Vectorise.py rebuild assets2d/_verify/logo --set 'palette.c1="#ff3366"'` wrote V_002 (parent V_001) with only the palette entry changed and V_001 untouched.

## Known limits

- The free-path refinement is slow on text: `glyphs` 364 s on one worker. Layers already run in parallel; a coarse-to-fine refinement would be the next lever.
- Gradients are fitted as SVG paint; blur is an SVG Gaussian filter, with shader-bank names recorded in `shader_hint` for the HyperFrames layer. A glow that is not a separate shape is folded into the background radial paint (case `glow`).
- No fitting loop yet that chains several frames of a motion; F2 is per still crop.

